<title>PORTUGAL: HOT-Banco Totta falls on resigning report.</title>
<headline>HOT-Banco Totta falls on resigning report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Banco Totta &amp; Acores (BTA) were falling nearly three percent to 3,113 escudos in early trade after a weekly newspaper reported that chairman Alipio Dias had resigned.</p>
<p>The stock was off an early low of 3,000 escudos.</p>
<p>There was no immediate comment from the bank on the report in Semanario Economico.  </p>
<p>According to the report, Luis Champalimaud, son of the head and founder of the Champalimaud group Antonio, could combine the chairmanship of both of the group's major banks, Banco Pinto &amp; Sotto Mayor and Banco Totta.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
